Version 2.4.0 brings support for properly building the plugin under MacOS
(as a VST3), new portamento modes, together with a couple of minor fixes
and cleanups.

Fixes:
- The RAL 5015 UI background color was incorrectly specified, resulting
  in the color being a bit darker than intended. The color now more closely
  matches the 'Sky Blue' description, but the difference is minor.
- When running on MacOS, the UI and credits splash screen were incorrectly
  rendered just as a grey window with no content. This has been fixed.
- A couple of minor optimizations in the Portamento function to slightly
  decrease DSP usage.

Features:
- New portamento modes: The classic exponentially asymptotical portamento
  (still default) has been supplemented with two linear modes: Linear Constant
  Rate (emulating the behavior on many Moog synthesizers such as the Minimoog),
  where the glide rate is constant regardless of the interval, which has the
  consequence that long intervals take longer to traverse than short ones.
  Finally, there is Linear Constant Time, where the rate is adjusted
  so that the time to traverse all intervals is the same. In this sense it
  mimics the classic mode, but with a linear ramp. The Constant Time mode
  takes the same time as the Constant Rate mode when the interval is
  one octave.
- Portamento start point: Traditionally on a polyphonic analog synthesizer,
  the voices start their portamento travel from the previously held pitch
  of the voice. This can result in a chaotic portamento experience (which
  can be useful in its own right). When the new Portamento Start parameter 
  is set to Track, the starting point for the portamento will be set to the
  pitch of the previously triggered voice, which gives a much more consistent
  and predictable portamento behavior in polyphonic modes.
- Added Github Action workfile to produce installation bundles for
  Mac (.pkg, VST3) and Linux (.deb and .rpm, LV2 and VST3).
- The DPF framework has been patched so that loading a preset in a VST
  or CLAP host which doesn't contain values for all parameters will result
  in the unspecified parameters to be set to their default values, rather
  than being left at their previous value, which is the default behavior.
- Added support for CLAP build; note that CLAP functionality has not been
  tested at this time.

Other changes:
- The Key Assign parameter group has been split into three separate
  groups for easier navigation and recognition. The actual parameters
  in the groups have not changed nor their order. This affects both the
  .ttl file specifying the groups (which is used for the parameter pages
  on the Zynthian platform) and the graphic UI. Note that in the graphic UI,
  the new Portamento mode parameters are in their own parameter group,
  beside the Portamento Time parameter.

As usual, a companion version 2.4.0z has been tagged on the Zynthian branch,
which supports the graphic envelope and filter display features in the Zynthian
UI.
